{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / immutable audit base\nAt `origin/main@88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684`, 19 shared test-support files contain exactly 51 editable prose blocks: 40 true leading docstrings and 11 full-line comment regions, 8,212 before-words. This rebases the prior 45-block plan: `tests/_engine_path.py` adds four blocks; `_git_upkeep.py` adds `D:init_bare_remote`; and `conftest.py` adds the canonical-engine-root rationale. Bracketed counts use `(?u)\\b[^\\W_]\\w*(?:[-'][^\\W_]\\w*)*\\b`.\n\n## Exact prose allowlist\n`D:<owner>` is a leading owner docstring; `C:<owner>:before:<anchor>` is one maximal full-line comment region before unchanged code. `@start-end[count]` gives the immutable span and word count.\n\n- `tests/_bank_observer.py` — `D:<module>@1-34[300]`, `D:make_observed_upsert@49-60[98]`, `D:make_response_counting_wrap@83-96[124]`, `D:bounded_bank_gaps@124-134[91]`.\n- `tests/_child_diag.py` — `D:assert_child_ran_clean@56-84[297]`, `D:assert_child_was_not_signal_killed@97-118[225]`.\n- `tests/_extra_guard.py` — `D:<module>@1-23[230]`.\n- `tests/_git_counts.py` — `D:<module>@1-13[121]`.\n- `tests/_git_floor.py` — `D:<module>@1-16[143]`.\n- `tests/_git_upkeep.py` — `D:<module>@1-57[518]`, `D:init_bare_remote@105-114[77]`.\n- `tests/_isolation.py` — `C:<module>:before:LEAK_WATCH_SUBDIRS@22-29[86]`, `C:<module>:before:GIT_PROBE_ATTEMPTS@33-46[152]`, `D:leak_failure_message@122-131[86]`, `D:head_move_failure_message@145-156[120]`, `D:working_tree_failure_message@176-184[78]`.\n- `tests/_jira_shape_contract.py` — `D:<module>@1-19[122]`.\n- `tests/_live_jira_confinement.py` — `D:<module>@1-23[200]`.\n- `tests/_log_integrity.py` — `D:<module>@1-44[416]`, `D:resto